# Half-Life HD gluon gun (Egon). Measured by hand off v_egon.mdl.
#
# Part J: "Continuous beam from the muzzle; the gun shudders in the hands
# through the physics. No hand reload."
#
# ONE CARD, THREE GAMEDIRS. valve_hd, gearbox_hd and bshift_hd ship three
# different v_egon.mdl FILES (160892, 198868 and 213104 bytes) but one rig:
# 49 bones, 11 sequences, the same bone names in the same order, and the same
# fingerprint 0xc9e21153. What differs between them is the arm and hand mesh,
# not the gun - the 518 body vertices and the 76 handle vertices are
# identical in all three, to the hundredth. The SD egons are NOT this card:
# valve is 32 bones / 0xa4ade1bd and gearbox and bshift are 31 / 0x1f521ab3.
#
# NO PRESET DESCRIBES THIS WEAPON. The six in dlls/vr_gun.cpp are
# magazine_slide, tube_pump, revolver, single_shot, thrown and belt. The egon
# has no magazine, no tube, no cylinder, nothing a hand lays in, nothing to
# throw and no belt: it draws from the uranium reserve like the gauss and the
# displacer. So no `type` line, and the joint below is declared directly, the
# way v_shock and v_displacer declare theirs.
#
# THE WEAPON FRAME is bone 11 `egon` - 518 of the model's 904 vertices
# (57.3%), parented to `Bip01 R Hand`, and the bone the model's single
# attachment sits on. That attachment is the muzzle, at (0, 0, 17.00), so +Z
# is forward along the beam. The body never moves in any of the 11
# sequences; the recoil shudder is in the arm bones, which is Part F's job,
# not a joint's. Weapon vertices run X -6.21..9.75, Y -2.41..5.48,
# Z 0.50..16.98 in that frame - a 24.26-unit diagonal.
#
# NO `fire` LINE, DELIBERATELY. The parser's default is semi, and that is
# closer to the truth than anything this card could write: the egon's primary
# is a held beam whose rate is the weapon's own code, not a sear cycling. An
# `auto rpm <n>` here would hang a second, invisible timer on a beam that has
# no cycle to time.
#
# NO `chamber`, NO `eject`, NO FEED FLAGS. There is no round, no case and no
# port anywhere on this mesh, and Part J gives the weapon no hand reload.
#
# NO `strike` LINE, so the weak pistol-whip default in vr_strike stands. Part
# J gives every firearm a butt-stroke with its own body; a measured one would
# need a head speed and a full-damage speed, and neither is a thing that can
# be measured off a model. Left to the default on purpose.

weapon v_egon
match  bones 49  seqs 11  hash 0xc9e21153

# JOINT 0: the fin on top of the receiver, and the only thing on this model
# that moves relative to the gun.
#
# `handle` is bone 12, a child of `egon` with 76 vertices (8.4%) - inside the
# plan's 3-10% candidate band - sitting at (0, 0, 7.947) with identity
# rotation, so its axes ARE the weapon's axes. It is a flat plate: 4.18 wide
# in X, 7.54 tall in Y, 0.88 thick in Z, standing about two units clear of
# the receiver's top at mid-barrel.
#
# A HINGE ABOUT THE BARREL. Its motion is one channel and one channel only -
# Z rotation, which in this frame is the beam axis - so the fin rocks over to
# one side and back rather than lifting. Span 0.5912 rad (33.9 degrees)
# across `fidget1`: 0 down to -0.5729 (32.8 degrees one way, frames 20-33)
# and back, with a 0.0183 flick the other way at frames 16-18. Travel is
# written as the span, 0.59, because that is the number the loader measures
# and compares against the 10% tolerance.
#
# IT MOVES IN `fidget1` AND NOWHERE ELSE. Not in idle1, not in any of the
# four fire sequences, not in altfireon/cycle/off, not in draw or holster.
# So this is a flourish, not a mechanism: nothing loads an egon and nothing
# can. It is declared anyway, for the reason v_shock's fin is declared - so
# the part is the simulator's to pose rather than the idle animation's, and
# so whatever drives the charge drives a part. Declaring it does mean the fin
# stops rocking by itself until something drives it; that is the trade, and
# it is the same trade the shock roach and the displacer already took.
#
# No spring, damping or recoil: the fin returns to rest in the animation, but
# an animation's ease-out is not a spring constant and there is nothing here
# to measure one from. Left at the parser's defaults.
#
# Grab point is the fin's own vertex centroid in the weapon frame,
# (0.02, 2.33, 7.91). Radius 2.5 reaches its full half-width (2.09) and both
# faces from there; the fin's HEIGHT is not the dimension a hand has to span.
joint 0  bone "handle"  hinge  travel 0.59  rest 0
    grab  point 0.02 2.33 7.91  radius 2.5
